# Files that must never enter this repository: model weights, host sync
# scratch, the Electron runtime, derived caches, and task scratch. Everything
# here is either large, regenerable in one command, or both. The comment on
# each group names the reason, because "why is this ignored" is the only
# question a reader ever asks of this file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights. This directory holds 9.0 GB across five GGUF files, mounted
# read only into the engine container at runtime. The repository carries the
# code that drives the weights and the records of what they scored, never the
# weights themselves. Resolved on this machine with:
#   models/gemma-4-E2B-it-Q4_K_M.gguf          3106738272
#   models/mmproj-F16.gguf                      985654080
#   models/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf   2019377600
#   models/Phi-3.5-mini-instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf   2393232672
#   models/qwen2.5-coder-1.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf 1117320768
# The bare patterns below also catch a weight file dropped at the root and the
# two stray empty directories named for weight files that a bad bind mount
# once created.
models/
*.gguf
*.ggml
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.h5
*.ckpt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Drive sync scratch. The single entry in .tmp.driveupload is a 2.9 GB
# hardlink to the gemma weights, which means it is one inode with two names:
# committing it would add a copy of a weight file, and deleting it would free
# nothing. Both directions of that are a reason to keep it out.
.tmp.drivedownload/
.tmp.driveupload/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Electron. The installed runtime is 321 MB, including a 100 MB plus framework
# binary and symlinked app bundles that git would store as link data or a
# second copy. The pinned versions live in package-lock.json and one
# `npm install` inside desktop/ restores the whole tree.
desktop/node_modules/
desktop/dist/
desktop/release/
desktop/out/

# Compiled artifacts. A static PHP binary is about 20 MB and is produced by
# the build recipe, not committed beside it.
*.phar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived caches. Model fingerprints and cache entries are recomputed from
# the weights and the source on demand, and a stale one is worse than none.
cache/

# Task scratch. workspace/ is bind mounted into the harness container as the
# task root and is rewritten by every run.
workspace/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Heavy media and archives. The four dated photographs are vision fixtures
# read from the host by absolute path; the JSON evidence records the path and
# the model's reading of it, not the bytes. The Kaggle cover images are the
# one exception, since they are small and are submission artifacts.
images/*.jpg
images/*.jpeg
images/*.png
images/*.heic
images/*.tif
images/*.mov
images/*.mp4
!images/jenny-jill-*.jpg
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
*.dmg
*.iso

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS. A .DS_Store is written into every directory the Finder touches, and
# this tree has picked up five of them.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.fseventsd
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
